s of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and June to July came in under 90% of normal in 34 of 75 years. In 2025, August to September came in at 49% of normal on the middle of the grids, and September to October at 69%. Grid 26913 had its driest year in 1965 at 69%. For 2026, a preliminary estimate on grid 27212 puts August to September at 76.0.</p>"}
